# ECC runtime state (hooks, governance state.db, continuous-learning, gateguard).
# The ecc-homunculus entries under the account dirs cover state left behind by the pre-#336
# layout only; live CLV2 state now sits at ~/.local/share/ecc-homunculus-<slug>. That path is
# outside chezmoi's target tree today, but it is ignored below anyway: observations.jsonl holds
# tool input/output whose redaction is best-effort, and this is a public repo, so a stray
# `chezmoi add` under ~/.local/share must not be able to pick it up.
#
# bash-commands.log is the same class of data — every Bash command this account ran, redacted
# on a best-effort basis — and was missing from this list. #496 removed its writer
# (hooks-fork/post-bash-command-log.js), which makes it an orphan that no longer changes and so
# no longer draws attention; the accumulated file itself is deliberately kept (#473 scopes that
# change to stopping new writes, not deleting history), which is exactly why it needs to be
# unreachable by a broad `chezmoi add`.
.local/share/ecc-homunculus-*
.claude/ecc
.claude/ecc-homunculus
.claude/.gateguard
.claude/bash-commands.log
.claude/mcp-health-cache.json
.claude/metrics

