# phone-harness agent workspace. run_onchange_after_19-setup-phone-harness.sh.tmpl
# creates this directory and ~/.zprofile points PH_AGENT_WORKSPACE at it, but its
# contents (agent_helpers.py) are written by the agent mid-session — chezmoi must
# neither deploy nor collect them. Ignored for the same reason as
# .local/share/ecc-homunculus-* above: this is a public repo, and a stray
# `chezmoi add` under ~/.local/share must not be able to pick up whatever an agent
# recorded while driving a real phone.
.local/share/phone-harness

# Improvement candidate queue state (#501, sub-issue of #473). Same reasoning as
# .local/share/ecc-homunculus-* and .local/share/phone-harness above: this is a public repo,
# and a stray `chezmoi add` under ~/.local/state must not be able to pick up the queue. The
# candidates summarise observed agent behaviour, the file is owner-only (0700 dir / 0600
# file) by design, and #473 AC-035 requires it never be published to Git or any external
# service. Its writer is ~/.local/lib/agent-improvement/, which manages the state itself.
.local/state/agent-improvement

